{"name":"Camel Hair","hex":"#dbb8a4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"camel hair","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of camelhair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camel_hair"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camel hair","blocks":[{"text":"Camel hair specifically refers to the fur from the body of a camel, but more generally refers to the fibre that may be made from either pure camel hair or a blend of camel hair and another fibre."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Bill_Blass_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel_hair"},{"title":"Brush","blocks":[{"text":"A brush is a common tool with bristles, wire, or other filaments. It generally comprises a handle or block to which filaments are affixed in either a parallel or perpendicular orientation, depending on the way the brush is to be gripped during use. The material of both the block and bristles or filaments is chosen to withstand hazards of its intended use, such as corrosive chemicals, heat, or abrasion. It is used for cleaning, grooming hair, makeup, painting, surface finishing, and many other purposes. It is one of the most basic and versatile tools in use today, and the average household may contain several dozen varieties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/BurglaryIsrael2.jpg/330px-BurglaryIsrael2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brush"},{"title":"Camel","blocks":[{"text":"A camel is an even-toed ungulate in the genus Camelus that bears distinctive fatty deposits known as \"humps\" on its back. Camels have long been domesticated and, as livestock, they provide food and textiles. Camels are working animals especially suited to their desert habitat and are a vital means of transport for passengers and cargo. There are three surviving species of camel. The one-humped dromedary makes up 94% of the world's camel population, and the two-humped Bactrian camel makes up 6%. The wild Bactrian camel is a distinct species that is not ancestral to the domestic Bactrian camel, and is now endangered, with around 1,000 individuals and a continuing decline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/07._Camel_Profile%2C_near_Silverton%2C_NSW%2C_07.07.2007.jpg/330px-07._Camel_Profile%2C_near_Silverton%2C_NSW%2C_07.07.2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel"},{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Camel_at_Givskud_Zoo.jpg/500px-Camel_at_Givskud_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Camel_at_Givskud_Zoo.jpg/1280px-Camel_at_Givskud_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Camel_at_Givskud_Zoo.jpg/500px-Camel_at_Givskud_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bactrian camel shedding its hair,  Givskud Zoo, Denmark","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACamel_at_Givskud_Zoo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Makeup_weapons_Brushes_.jpg/500px-Makeup_weapons_Brushes_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Makeup_weapons_Brushes_.jpg/1280px-Makeup_weapons_Brushes_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Makeup_weapons_Brushes_.jpg/500px-Makeup_weapons_Brushes_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Assorted cosmetics and Makeup brushes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMakeup_weapons_Brushes_.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Camels_by_country_per_capita.png/500px-Camels_by_country_per_capita.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Camels_by_country_per_capita.png/1280px-Camels_by_country_per_capita.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Camels_by_country_per_capita.png/500px-Camels_by_country_per_capita.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACamels_by_country_per_capita.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG/500px-2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG/1280px-2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG/500px-2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG?utm_source=e